import{_ as t,o,c as s,a0 as n}from"./chunks/framework.D4fUSYzX.js";const l=JSON.parse('{"title":"ADR 0127: The plane pushes its own branches outside the contributor pre-push hook","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"adr/0127-the-plane-pushes-its-own-branches-outside-the-contributor-pre-push-hook.md","filePath":"adr/0127-the-plane-pushes-its-own-branches-outside-the-contributor-pre-push-hook.md"}'),a={name:"adr/0127-the-plane-pushes-its-own-branches-outside-the-contributor-pre-push-hook.md"};function h(r,e,c,i,d,p){return o(),s("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[n('<h1 id="adr-0127-the-plane-pushes-its-own-branches-outside-the-contributor-pre-push-hook" tabindex="-1">ADR 0127: The plane pushes its own branches outside the contributor pre-push hook <a class="header-anchor" href="#adr-0127-the-plane-pushes-its-own-branches-outside-the-contributor-pre-push-hook" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;ADR 0127: The plane pushes its own branches outside the contributor pre-push hook&quot;">​</a></h1><p>Status: accepted Date: 2026-10-09 Records that the control plane&#39;s own <code>git push</code> commands bypass <code>scripts/git-hooks/pre-push</code>. It changes no check: the hook, its two checks, and its behind rule stand unchanged for a contributor&#39;s push (ADR 0105), and CI runs the same checks on what the plane pushes.</p><h2 id="context" tabindex="-1">Context <a class="header-anchor" href="#context" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Context&quot;">​</a></h2><p><a href="./0105-the-push-gate-runs-the-three-checks-on-the-merged-tree-and-a-hook-owns-the-two-cheap-ones.html">ADR 0105</a> put <code>bun run lint</code>, <code>bun run typecheck</code>, and a behind rule into <code>scripts/git-hooks/pre-push</code>, active in a checkout that set <code>core.hooksPath</code>. The ADR placed that gate at the moment a contributor pushes work for review. It did not say what happens when the control plane pushes.</p><p>The plane pushes two things of its own:</p><ul><li>the ticket&#39;s factory branch, carrying only the hold commit the pull request open puts under it (ADR 0076), pushed from the Shared checkout;</li><li>a Repository init&#39;s first commit (ADR 0075), pushed from a throwaway worktree.</li></ul><p><code>core.hooksPath</code> is a repository setting, not a worktree setting, so the hook runs on those pushes too, and it answers for whatever tree it happens to stand in. Two measurements on this machine show what that costs.</p><ul><li>The Shared checkout&#39;s <code>node_modules</code> predated <code>@types/fontkit</code>, which landed in <code>6dff8d75</code> on 2026-10-08. <code>bun run typecheck</code> failed with TS7016 on <code>scripts/screen-font.ts</code>, the hook refused, and every Handoff of a task type that opens a pull request failed at its branch push. The operator&#39;s warning read <code>pushing the factory branch factory/352-... failed: error: failed to push some refs to &#39;https://github.com/SeriousJul/my-little-software-factory.git&#39;</code>. The plane keeps one line of a failed command, the one a tool marks with <code>error:</code> or <code>fatal:</code> (<code>failureLine</code> in <code>src/lines.ts</code>), so the hook&#39;s written reason - <code>pre-push: bun run typecheck failed</code> - never reached the operator.</li><li>18 of this repository&#39;s herdr worktrees hold no <code>node_modules</code>. In one of them, <code>bun run lint</code> exits 127 with <code>biome: command not found</code>, so the hook refuses a push made from a fresh worktree as well.</li></ul><p>Neither failure is about the commits being pushed. The hold commit stands on <code>origin/&lt;default branch&gt;</code>, which CI already proved green, and the init commit is generated bytes the plane wrote into a throwaway worktree.</p><h2 id="decision" tabindex="-1">Decision <a class="header-anchor" href="#decision" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Decision&quot;">​</a></h2><p><strong>The plane&#39;s pushes name the bypass at the call site, and the bypass is one constant.</strong></p><p><code>src/git-push.ts</code> holds <code>BYPASS_CONTRIBUTOR_PUSH_HOOK</code>, the single flag git documents for skipping the pre-push hook: <code>--no-verify</code>. Every push the plane builds spreads it into its argv:</p><ul><li><code>pushFactoryBranch</code> in <code>src/handoff.ts</code>, the factory branch push of ADR 0076;</li><li><code>commitAndPushInit</code> in <code>src/repo-init.ts</code>, the init push of ADR 0075.</li></ul><p><strong>The hook keeps its whole rule for a contributor.</strong> ADR 0105 stands, and the instruction not to bypass the hook with <code>--no-verify</code> still governs the work a person or an Agent pushes from a checkout. The Agent&#39;s own pushes are contributor pushes and keep the gate.</p><p><strong>The rule is checked from both sides.</strong> <code>test/handoff.test.ts</code> and <code>test/repo-init.test.ts</code> pin the argv each flow sends, read from the constant so a change to the rule moves one place. <code>test/git-push-architecture.test.ts</code> refuses a <code>&quot;git&quot;</code> push argv in <code>src</code> whose file does not name the constant, so a third push cannot be written without it.</p><h2 id="considered-options" tabindex="-1">Considered options <a class="header-anchor" href="#considered-options" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Considered options&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Repair the checkout and change no code.</strong> Rejected: <code>bun install</code> restores this run, not the rule. Any red lint, red typecheck, or uninstalled dependency in the Shared checkout stops every Handoff again, and the warning names none of them.</li><li><strong>Make the hook skip its checks when the dependencies are missing.</strong> Rejected: the hook then stops gating without saying so, and the plane still depends on a hook a fresh clone never installed.</li><li><strong>Let the hook detect the plane&#39;s push through an environment marker.</strong> Rejected: a marker any contributor can set is not a gate, and the plane&#39;s argv would state nothing about what it skipped.</li><li><strong>Unset <code>core.hooksPath</code> in the plane&#39;s checkout.</strong> Rejected: it removes the contributor gate from the one checkout that needs it most.</li><li><strong>Report the hook&#39;s reason instead.</strong> Rejected as the fix and settled by the decision: once the plane&#39;s push names the bypass, no local check stands in its path, so there is no hidden reason left to report.</li></ul><h2 id="consequences" tabindex="-1">Consequences <a class="header-anchor" href="#consequences" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Consequences&quot;">​</a></h2><p>A Handoff no longer depends on the Shared checkout&#39;s dependency install, nor on whether that checkout&#39;s lint and typecheck are clean. The checks for what the plane pushes belong where they already ran: the draft pull request the push creates gets <code>bun run lint</code>, <code>bun run typecheck</code>, and <code>bun run test</code> from CI.</p><p>The plane&#39;s push path runs no local check of its own. That is the point of the decision, and it is worth stating plainly: the plane&#39;s push is a bookkeeping act that makes the branch a pull request can stand on, not a submission of work.</p><p><code>docs/development/quality-gate.md</code>, <code>docs/development/commands.md</code>, and <code>AGENTS.md</code> now name who the hook gates. The hook&#39;s own header says the same.</p><p>What was measured, and what was not, stands in <a href="https://github.com/SeriousJul/my-little-software-factory/blob/main/docs/verification/contributor-push-gate.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">the verification record</a>.</p>',22)])])}const f=t(a,[["render",h]]);export{l as __pageData,f as default};
